  <arrangement id="6186b9ce8bb24846518875b41ed438a1">
    <head>Arrangement</head>
<p>This collection is divided into four series:</p><p>Series 1 - Tennessee</p><p>Series 2 - Rockefeller Interests</p><p>Series 3 - Personal Interests</p><p>Series 4 - Wickliffe Rose photographs</p>  </arrangement>
  <userestrict id="54205ff2744d4ed0b1cc67dfe9e65f38">
    <head>Conditions Governing Use</head>
<p>Rockefeller Foundation has title, copyright, and literary rights in the collection, in so far as it holds them. Rockefeller Archive Center has authority to grant permission to cite and publish archival material from the collection.</p>  </userestrict>
  <scopecontent id="9d166abbc17c372f774ed3f21d08d67b">
    <head>Scope and Contents note</head>
<p>Important subjects in this collection include Rose's election to Peabody College Presidency, Peabody Fund Award, International Health Division, travels, and fishing.</p><p>Among the correspondents are Victor G. Heiser; Abraham Flexner; George Clarke; Trevor Arnett; John D. Rockefeller, Jr.; A. E. Shipley; Wickliffe Rose; Frederick T. Gates; and John Ferrell.</p>  </scopecontent>
  <processinfo id="8499f5f6312d8143e430f87e30e8d7b4">
    <head>Processing Information note</head>
<p>Processing was completed as of May 19, 1969.  Processing Level 3: Standard Processing.  All material is available in acid free manuscript boxes and folders.</p>  </processinfo>
  <acqinfo id="20364fae02a9c5d17171be624bfb9a46">
    <head>Immediate Source of Acquisition note</head>
<p>The papers of Wickliffe Rose were deposited with The Rockefeller Foundation Archives in December 1966 and October 1968, by Harold Wickliffe Rose.</p>  </acqinfo>
